From 5290a4c410907c81fff5bc9315e5b4a26fa26a8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "herve.marchal" <herve.marchal@developpement-durable.gouv.fr>
Date: Wed, 4 Feb 2026 21:37:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] patch(offline): Add exposed wheels mode with multi-Python
 support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Introduce new installation architecture to avoid massive ZIP downloads:
- Wheels exposed in dist-offline/wheels/ (accessible via URL/Git)
- Smart install_offline.py downloads only compatible wheels
- Supports Python 3.10, 3.11, 3.12 automatically
- Old ZIP mode preserved with --mode zip option

Changes:
- scripts/build_offline_package.py:
  * Add --mode argument (zip|exposed, default: exposed)
  * Add build_exposed_package() for new architecture
  * Add multi-version Python download (3.10, 3.11, 3.12)
  * Refactor build_zip_package() for old mode
  * Update documentation with troubleshooting section

- dist-offline/install_offline.py: NEW
  * Detects Python version automatically
  * Downloads only compatible wheels via pip download
  * Installs dependencies in correct order
  * Handles greenlet and other binary deps correctly

- dist-offline/uninstall_offline.py: NEW
  * Clean uninstall with --keep-deps option
  * Removes dependencies in reverse order

Benefits:
- No 80MB ZIP download required
- Users download only ~10KB scripts
- Automatic version detection and compatibility
- Bandwidth efficient
- Works with any Python 3.10+

Usage:
  # Build exposed wheels (new default)
  python scripts/build_offline_package.py

  # Build ZIP package (old mode)
  python scripts/build_offline_package.py --mode zip

Fixes Python version mismatch errors (cp310 vs cp311 wheels).

